Payment API

Channels:

  REST:
    base: /api/v1/payments

  Internal:
    PaymentService

  Events:
    payment.created
    payment.completed
    payment.refunded

Endpoints:

  POST   /payments
  GET    /payments/:id
  POST   /payments/:id/refund

Ownership:

  POST /payments
    -> BE.Payment.Create

  GET /payments/:id
    -> BE.Payment.Get

  POST /payments/:id/refund
    -> BE.Payment.Refund

Services:

  PaymentService
    BE:  ./backend/payment/service.go
    Produces:    Payment API
    ConsumedBy:  FE.PaymentScreen, MD.PaymentScreen, QA.PaymentFlow

Errors:

  PAY-REF-001
    Channel:    POST /payments/:id/refund
    Backend:    Payment.Refund
    DB:         payment_transactions
    Consumers:  FE.PaymentDetails, MD.PaymentDetails
    QA:         payment/refund

Note:
  A user report like "Refund düyməsində error çıxır" resolves directly to
  an error code's affected graph (channel -> BE -> DB -> FE/MD -> QA)
  instead of the AI guessing where to look (prompt/new/9.md, point 7).
